From: ANGI build integration
Subject: [PATCH] Retain safe open fallback when toolchain headers lack openat2

The appliance kernel is new enough for openat2, but its external toolchain
uses older syscall headers. In that case syscall_openat2 always returns
ENOSYS, so retain bubblewrap's existing safe fallback even when the assumed
kernel version is recent. Sandbox restrictions remain enabled.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/safe_openat.c
+++ b/safe_openat.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 
 bool opt_force_openat_fallback = false;
 
-#if ASSUMED_KERNEL < BWRAP_KERNEL_VERSION (5, 6, 0)
+#if ASSUMED_KERNEL < BWRAP_KERNEL_VERSION (5, 6, 0) || !defined(__NR_openat2)
 #  define USE_OPENAT_FALLBACK 1
 #else
 #  define USE_OPENAT_FALLBACK 0
